================================================================================
Vendored cores and the licence of a built image
================================================================================

The MIT terms above cover the first-party code in this repository: everything
under src/, include/ (except include/peanut_gb.h), lib/gbcore/, lib/gb_runner/,
test/ and tools/. lib/minigb_apu/ is third-party under its own permissive
terms; see lib/minigb_apu/LICENSE.

Two emulator cores are vendored, and exactly one is linked into any given
firmware image. Which one you build decides the licence of that image.

  include/peanut_gb.h  Peanut-GB, MIT, copyright 2018-2023 Mahyar Koshkouei.
                       An image built with this core is distributed under MIT.
                       This is the default core and the `cyd` environment.

  lib/gnuboy/          gnuboy, as carried by retro-go, GPL-2.0-or-later. See
                       lib/gnuboy/COPYING for the full text and
                       lib/gnuboy/CREDITS for authorship. An image built with
                       this core is a combined work with GPL-2.0 code, so that
                       image is distributed under GPL-2.0-or-later, and anyone
                       distributing it owes the corresponding source under
                       those terms. This is the `cyd-gnuboy` environment.

The MIT grant on the first-party code is unaffected either way: it stays MIT at
the source level, and the GPL obligation attaches only to the combined image
that links lib/gnuboy/.
